                </h5>Significant Places and Regions</h5>
                <p>
    <ol>
        <li>Abuja: The Federal Capital Territory, located in the center of the country, known for landmarks like Aso Rock and the National Mosque.</li>
        <li>Lagos: The former capital, economic heart, and largest city in Africa, known for its intense energy, nightlife, and bustling industries.</li>
        <li>Kano: A major commercial hub in the north with a rich history centered on the Great Mosque and traditional dye pits.</li>
        <li>Port Harcourt: A crucial city in the Niger Delta, central to Nigeria’s oil and gas industry.</li>
        <li>Jos Plateau: Known for a cooler climate and diverse ethnic groups.</li>
        <li>Obudu Plateau/Gashaka Gumti National Park: Located in the east, these feature high mountains and rainforests.</li>
        <li>Benin City: Historic capital of the ancient Benin Empire, known for its bronze casting and walls.</li>
    </ol>
</p>


